1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Fedor Prokofievich Sokovnin (d. 1697) - Russian statesman, Steward (1647), Butler (1669), dumnyi nobleman (1670), courtier (1676) and lord (1682). The representative of the noble family Sokovnin. The eldest son oko
2 CONC lnichy and magistrates Prokofy Fedorovich Sokovnin (? - 1662) and Anissya Nikitichny Naumova. Younger brother - Alexei Prokofievich Sokovnin courtier. January 6, 1647 FP Sokovnin was granted to the king's attendants. In January of
2 CONC  the same year during the first wedding of Tsar Alexei Mikhailovich Mary Ilyinichna Myloslavska he was among the ride. In 1648 and 1650 respectively steward FP Sokovnin accompanied by Tsar Alexei Mikhailovich in his country trips.
2 CONC  In 1658-1660 years he served at the king's table during the reception of the Georgian prince Nikolai Davidovich, in 1664 when receiving the English ambassador. From a letter of Patriarch Nikon to the famous Guardian Education in 
2 CONC Moscow Fyodor Rtishchev in 1663 it is clear that Fedor Sokovnin was in a relationship, as the patriarch and with Rtishchev. In the years 1668-1671 FP Sokovnin present in the Artisan Chamber of Queen Mary Ilinichny, in 1669 was als
2 CONC o her butler. In 1670 Fedor Prokofievich Sokovnin was granted from the butlers in the duma nobles. In 1675 there was a Commander in Chuguev. At the beginning of the reign of Tsar Fedor Alekseevich in 1676, when the disgraced noble
2 CONC man Artamon Matveyev was sent to Silesia in Verkhoturye, in pursuit of them were sent from the capital of several persons, including FP Sokovnin. In the same 1676 was granted to the courtiers. In 1677, FP Sokovnin attended the Wor
2 CONC kshop Chamber Queen Natalia. In 1676-1682 years he accompanied the king Fedor Alekseevich in his country trips. In 1677, at the request of Tsar Fedor Alekseevich, Fedor Sokovnin found for the five-year Tsarevich Peter I the teache
2 CONC r. They became Nikita Zotov, clerk Pleas order. In 1680, the king Fedor Alekseevich ordered to him to let the drug in the mansions Queen Natalia and Prince Peter Alekseevich. In 1681 he signed with the Boyar Prince Nikita Ivanovic
2 CONC h Odoyevsky and boyars Ivan Mikhailovich Miloslavsky on the row entry Prince Semen Jurevicha Zvenigorod. In 1682 Fedor Sokovnin signed the conciliar decree on the destruction of localism. June 29 of the same in 1682 it was granted
2 CONC  to the boyars. Then, for almost fifteen years, his name is rarely found in the ranks when he was in Moscow in religious processions, or accompanied by the kings of John and Peter out of town. March 20, 1697 after the execution of
2 CONC  his brother Alexis Fedor Prokofievich Sokovnin was sent into exile in distant villages, but without depriving the title of nobleman. With him is banished his wife and children. Was married twice. From his first marriage had three
2 CONC  sons, and the second marriage - a son and three daughters: Fedor Fedorovich Sokovnin (? - 1698), the room steward (1676-1697). Peter F. Sokovnin (d. After 1714), the room steward (1692-1697). Prokofi F. Sokovnin, room steward (16
2 CONC 92-1697). Nikita Fedorovich Sokovnin (? - 1770), Major General (1741), Lieutenant-General (1755), the general-in-chief and Commander of the Order of St. Alexander Nevsky Irina Fedorovna Sokovnin Maria Feodorovna Sokovnin Anna Feod
2 CONC orovna Sokovnin, 1st wife steward, Prince Peter D. Shcherbatova (d. 1724)
