1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ivan Betskoy was the illegitimate son of Prince Ivan Trubetskoy and his Swedish mistress, Baroness von Wrede, conceived Commandant Troubetskoy was held as a prisoner of war in Sweden following the Russian surrender
2 CONC  at the Battle of Narva during the Azov Campaigns His surname is the abbreviated form of his father's "Troubetskoy" "Betskoy"(also written as Betsky, and Betski)
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Stockholm, where Prince Trubetskoy was held captive throughout the Great Northern War until his return to Russia after a prisoner exchange in 1718. Ivan Betskoy was sent to Copenhagen for a military education and th
2 CONC en joined an elite cavalry regiment. It was in the Danish service that he sustained a fall from a horse which forced him to retire from the service. Field Marshal Trubetskoy, having no other sons but Betskoy, summoned him to Russi
2 CONC a in 1729. At first he served as his father's aide-de-camp but later would be sent on diplomatic missions to various capitals of Europe. Ivan Betskoy was actively involved in a coup d'etat that brought Elizaveta Petrovna to the Ru
2 CONC ssian throne. The grateful empress promoted him to General Major and asked him to attend Joanna Elisabeth of Holstein-Gottorp, whose daughter Catherine was selected as a bride for the Empress' nephew and heir, Grand Duke Peter. In
2 CONC  truth, Betskoy had been on friendly terms with Johanna Elisabeth for two decades previous, their intimacy giving rise to rumours that Catherine was his biological daughter.
